1 NOTE From Wikipedia: "In the early 17th century, Martaizé, along with the nearby village of La Chaussée, was one of the seigneuries of Charles de Menou d'Aulnay. Several of the earliest settlers of Acadia including the Gaudets, LeBlancs, the Bourgs, th
2 CONC e Terriots, and the Savoies are believed to have been recruited by d'Aulnay from their original home in Martaizé to colonize New France. [1]"
2 CONT    
2 CONT Either Guillaume or his wife Huguette is a descendant of Cardinal Villenueve, ancestor of Sir Charles A.P. Peletier.
2 CONT The Blanchards were freeholders of the seigneurie (Manor or lordship) of Aulnay, property of the mother of Charles de Menou de Charnisoy, Lord of Aulnay; situated at Martaize, near Loudin, France.
2 CONT RIN: MH:N501016
2 CONT REFN: 14 DEC 2015 16:11:29
