1 NOTE Marriage to Miss Pyari by Rev. Phifer, at Lead Jan 31 1882.  Could this be a misspelling of Pajari?  First name is Matilda, just like first wife.  Black Hills Daily Times Jan 31, 1882.  P.1, Col.4
2 CONT    
2 CONT Delinquent tax sale of Spring Creek advertised Sept. 5, 1885 - whole town?  Home there? Black Hills Daily Times Sept 5, 1885, P.3, Col.2
2 CONT    
2 CONT Arrives in Deadwood 1880.  Black Hills Daily Times Aug. 6, 1880 P.4, Col.5
2 CONT    
2 CONT According to Elsie Gorder he died while going out to get the cows one day of a heart attack.
2 CONT    
2 CONT Elsie Gorder found a paper her mother had written giving a brief history of Simon: "Simon Hellman, my father, was born in Paavolla Finland. When a young man 19 years old joined the navy and sailed ocean blue for 10 years then came to America and se
2 CONC ttled in Calumet, Mich. Worked in copper mine.When the gold rush was on in the Black Hills, Lead SD, he ame out and worked in Homestake. My mother Mathilda Bajari also came out from Calumet, the were married.  he then filed homestead, 160 acres wes
2 CONC t of Bear Butte. Farmed and raised cattle. Nov. 14, 1888, he herded cattle out of corn field towards the Butte, fell dead of heart trouble. Mother married again, moved to Terraville. I got my education there then moved to Lead. I was married Sept
2 CONC . 14, 1901."
2 CONT RIN: MH:N29
2 CONT REFN: 14 DEC 2015 16:11:29
