1 OBJE @O270@
1 NOTE Christened December 2, 1866 in Parikkala, Viipuri, Finland.
2 CONT Step mother came to America when her father died.  She was about 14.
2 CONT From Lead Daily (Lead, South Dakota) Wed., April 7, 1926.
2 CONT "MRS. ELSA HILDEN PASSES AWAY AT DAUGHTER'S HOME
2 CONT The death of Mrs. Elsa Mathilda Hilden occurred last evening at the home of her daughter, at 24 Haggin Avenue. Funeral arrangements have not yet been completed.  Elsa Mathilda Hilden was born in Finland, October 8, 1850, and moved to Norway in 1858
2 CONC . She came to Calumet, Michigan, in 1874, moving to Lead in 1881. The following year she married Simon Hellman.  A daughter, Mrs. Ida Leh-to, being born to this union. Mr. Hellman passed away in 1888 and she was married to Otto Hilden in August 188
2 CONC 9. She is survived by a daughter and four grandchildren, Reuben Lehto, Helen Lehto, Elnora Lehto, and Mrs. V.C. Linstrom."
2 CONT    
2 CONT 0  0  1  99  568  Northern Michigan University  4  1  666  14.0     
