1 NOTE Johan Staël von Holstein was born in 1636 in Livonia then belonged to Sweden. His military career the Royal Swedish arm he began in 1651. The October 14, 1652, he was naturalized along with his brothers and cousins ​​Swedish nobleman by Queen Chris
2 CONC tina. The was introduced at the Swedish House of Nobility September 20, 1675 under the name Staël von Holstein No: 834. Johan was appointed in 1658 to the quartermaster general at the Swedish arm in Denmark. On September 6, 1660 he was promoted t
2 CONC o Major in the Artillery work in Ingria. He married in 1664 with Christina Möller. On 15 September 1673 he was appointed lieutenant colonel in the artillery in Finland. During his time in Estonia and Ingria worked Johan inspector of fortifikationsa
2 CONC rbetet in Estonia and Ingria. Among other bail Nyenschanz that was where St. Petersburg is located today. Johan Staël von Holstein owned estates Wasahof, Goldina in Waiwara parish in Estonia and Lilie Hagen Gregorii parish in Koporie County and Dud
2 CONC erhof in Gregori parish in Nöteborgs County. All the property was in Ingria.
