2 _APID 12157945241:1030:28955631
1 NOTE According to the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy, the origins of this wife of Rotbald II are unknown; there is no indication in this most trusted source that she was the daughter of Boson I de la Marche (or that Boson had a daughter with this nam
2 CONC e), so if this parentage is still linked it is probably not correct.
2 CONT 
2 CONT Although records indicate a wife of Rotbald II named Ermengarde followed by Emilde followed by Ermengarde, some scholars believe that all of these references refer to one wife. Moreover, Szabolcs de Vajay suggests that she was Emilde de Gévaudan, d
2 CONC aughter of Etienne Vicomte de Gévaudan &amp;amp; his first wife Anne; Europäische Stammtafeln identifies her as Ermengarde (-25 or 27 Aug after 1057), who married secondly ([24 Apr/28 Jul] 1011) as his second wife, Rudolf III King of Burgundy.
