2 CONC ;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;Three orphaned Boudrot boys&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;Brot
2 CONC hers Pierre Poirier and Jean Baptiste Poirier sons of Michel Poirier and Marie Boudrot married sisters.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;Pierre married Agnes Marie Cormier&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&
2 CONC gt;Jean- Baptiste married Marie Angelique Cormier&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;A third sister Marie Madeleine Cormier married Pierre and Jean-Baptiste&amp;rsquo;s uncle Michel Boudrot, brother to their mother Marie Boudro
2 CONC t.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;Sometime before the 1714 census Marie Madeleine and Michel Boudrot died. On the 1714 census their 3 youngest sons&lt;span style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Claude, Pau
2 CONC l and Anselme are shown as orphans.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;Paul was taken in by Pierre Poirier and Agnes Cormier&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;Anselme was taken in by Jean Baptiste Poirie
