1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&amp;nbsp;Eerikki was born in 1500 at the end, and the next century&amp;#39;s first half, he founded a family. &lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="direction: ltr; text-align: "&gt;Oliko h&amp;auml;n talollinen, porvari tai kenti
2 CONC es pappi, ei tiedet&amp;auml;.&lt;/span&gt; Was he talollinen, bourgeois, or perhaps a priest, it is not known.&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="direction: ltr; text-align: "&gt;On arveltu, ett&amp;auml; h&amp;auml;n olisi ollut helsinkil&a
2 CONC mp;auml;inen [2], mutta siit&amp;auml; ei ole varmuutta.&lt;/span&gt; It is said that he would have been in Helsinki [2], but it is not certain.&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="direction: ltr; text-align: "&gt;Joka tapauksessa h&amp;auml;
2 CONC n oli varakas ja edistysmielinen, koska koulutti papin pojastaan, joka tunnettiin nimell&amp;auml; Israel Erici Argillander.&lt;/span&gt; In any case, he was a wealthy and progressive, because the priest, trained his son, who was known as Israel Er
2 CONC ici Argillander.&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="direction: ltr; text-align: "&gt;Sukukirjassaan [1] Axel Bergholm kertoo laajasti Savon Argillander-suvusta ja toteaa, ett&amp;auml; Israel Erici ei ole sukua savolaisille Argillandereille.&
2 CONC lt;/span&gt; Relatives In his book [1] Axel Bergholm tells widely Savon Argillander-genus, and notes that Israel Erici is not related to the savola Argillandereille.&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="direction: ltr; text-align: "&gt;H&amp;au
2 CONC ml;n mainitsee muitakin Argillandereita, joiden sukujohtoa h&amp;auml;n ei ollut pystynyt selvitt&amp;auml;m&amp;auml;&amp;auml;n.&lt;/span&gt; He cites other Argillandereita whose sex cord he had not been able to clarify.&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span&gt;
2 CONC &lt;span style="direction: ltr; text-align: "&gt;Kristiinankaupungissa eli lautturiperhe Argillander, Oulussa tullikirjuri Argillander, hevossepp&amp;auml; Johan Argillander muutti 1756 Vaasasta Kristiinankaupunkiin, Turussa vaikutti 1700-luvun puo
2 CONC liv&amp;auml;liss&amp;auml; kaksi Argillander-nimist&amp;auml; vaskisepp&amp;auml;&amp;auml;, my&amp;ouml;s Ruotsissa oli Argilladereita, joista l&amp;ouml;ytyy mainintoja mm.&lt;/span&gt; Kristinestad ie lautturiperhe Argillander, Oulu tullikirjur
2 CONC i Argillander horse blacksmith Johan Argillander moved in 1756 from Vaasa Kristiinan city, Turku, appeared mid-1700&amp;#39;s two-Argillander names vaskisepp&amp;auml;&amp;auml;, also in Sweden was Argilladereita, which contain references to such.&
2 CONC lt;/span&gt; &lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="direction: ltr; text-align: "&gt;Str&amp;auml;ngn&amp;auml;sin hiippakunnan paimenmuistiosta.&lt;/span&gt; Str&amp;auml;ngn&amp;auml;s diocesan pastoral memo.&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="directi
2 CONC on: ltr; text-align: "&gt;N&amp;auml;ytt&amp;auml;&amp;auml;, ett&amp;auml; Argillander on ollut ja on edelleen hieno nimi ja se on otettu k&amp;auml;ytt&amp;ouml;&amp;ouml;n eri puolilla Ruotsin valtakuntaa.&lt;/span&gt; It seems that Argillande
2 CONC r has been and still is a great name, and it has been introduced in various parts of the Swedish Empire.&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="direction: ltr; text-align: "&gt;Keski-Suomen ja Savon Argillanderit eiv&amp;auml;t taida olla sukua k
2 CONC esken&amp;auml;&amp;auml;n.&lt;/span&gt; Central Finland and Savo Argillanderit are likely to be related to each other&lt;/span&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
