2 CONC ;[13]&lt;/sup&gt;&amp;nbsp;who were perhaps drawn by the marshy Aachen basin's&amp;nbsp;hot sulphur springs&amp;nbsp;where they worshiped&amp;nbsp;Grannus, god of light and healing.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin: 0.5em 0px; line-height
2 CONC : inherit;"&gt;Later, the 25-hectare Roman spa resort town of&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;Aquae Granni&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;was, according to legend, founded by Grenus, under&amp;nbsp;Hadrian, in&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;ca&lt;/em&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style="fon
2 CONC t-variant: small-caps;"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style="font-variant: small-caps;"&gt;d&lt;/span&gt;. 124. Instead, the fictitious founder refers to the Celtic god, and it seems it was the Roman 6th Legion at the start of the 1st century that fir
2 CONC st channelled the hot springs into a spa at B&amp;uuml;chel,&lt;sup style="line-height: 1; font-size: 11.1999998092651px; unicode-bidi: -webkit-isolate;"&gt;[nb 2]&lt;/sup&gt;adding at the end of the same century the&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;M&amp;uuml;n
2 CONC stertherme&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;spa,&lt;sup style="line-height: 1; font-size: 11.1999998092651px; unicode-bidi: -webkit-isolate;"&gt;[15]&lt;/sup&gt;&amp;nbsp;two water pipelines, and a likely sanctuary dedicated to Grannus. A kind of forum, surroun
2 CONC ded by colonnades, connected the two spa complexes. There was also an extensive residential area, part of it inhabited by a flourished Jewish community.&lt;sup style="line-height: 1; font-size: 11.1999998092651px; unicode-bidi: -webkit-isolate;"&gt
2 CONC ;[16]&lt;/sup&gt;&amp;nbsp;The Romans built bathhouses near&amp;nbsp;Burtscheid. A temple precinct called&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;Vernenum&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;was built near the modern&amp;nbsp;Kornelim&amp;uuml;nster/Walheim. Today, remains have been f
