2 CONC &lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin: 0.5em 0px; line-height: inherit;"&gt;Roman civil administration fell apart in Aachen between the end of the 4th and beginning of the 5th centuries. Rome withdrew its troops from the area but the town rema
2 CONC ined populated. By 470, the town came to be ruled by the&amp;nbsp;Ripuarian Franks&lt;sup style="line-height: 1; font-size: 11.1999998092651px; unicode-bidi: -webkit-isolate;"&gt;[18]&lt;/sup&gt;and subordinated to their capital,&amp;nbsp;Cologne.&
