2 CONC bsp;Einhard&amp;nbsp;mentions that in 765&amp;ndash;6 Pepin spent both Christmas and Easter at&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;Aquis villa&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;("&lt;span&gt;Et celebravit natalem Domini in Aquis villa et pascha similiter.&lt;/span&gt;"),&lt;su
2 CONC p style="line-height: 1; font-size: 11.1999998092651px; unicode-bidi: -webkit-isolate;"&gt;[20]&lt;/sup&gt;&amp;nbsp;which must have been sufficiently equipped to support the royal household for several months. In the year of his coronation as Kin
2 CONC g of Franks, 768,&amp;nbsp;Charlemagne&amp;nbsp;came to spend Christmas at Aachen for the first time.&lt;sup style="line-height: 1; font-size: 11.1999998092651px; unicode-bidi: -webkit-isolate;"&gt;[nb 3]&lt;/sup&gt;&amp;nbsp;He went on to remain t
2 CONC here in a&amp;nbsp;mansion&amp;nbsp;which he may have extended, although there is no source attesting to any significant building activity at Aachen in his time, apart from the building of the&amp;nbsp;Palatine Chapel in Aachen&amp;nbsp;(since 1929
2 CONC , cathedral) and the palatial presentation halls. Charlemagne spent most winters in Aachen between 792 and his death in 814. Aachen became the focus of his court and the political centre of his empire. After his death, the king was buried in the ch
2 CONC urch which he had built;&lt;sup style="line-height: 1; font-size: 11.1999998092651px; unicode-bidi: -webkit-isolate;"&gt;[22]&lt;/sup&gt;&amp;nbsp;his original tomb has been lost, while his alleged remains are preserved in the shrine where he was r
2 CONC eburied after being declared a saint; his saintliness, however, was never very widely acknowledged outside. In 936,&amp;nbsp;Otto I&amp;nbsp;was crowned king of&amp;nbsp;East Francia&amp;nbsp;in the collegiate church built by Charlemagne. While&amp
2 CONC ;nbsp;Otto II&amp;nbsp;ruled, the nobles revolted and the&amp;nbsp;West Franks, underLothair,&lt;sup style="line-height: 1; font-size: 11.1999998092651px; unicode-bidi: -webkit-isolate;"&gt;[23]&lt;/sup&gt;&amp;nbsp;raided Aachen in the ensuing con
