2 CONC .5em 0px; line-height: inherit;"&gt;Aachen has proven an important site for the production of historical manuscripts. Under Charlemagne's purview, both theAda Gospels&amp;nbsp;and the&amp;nbsp;Coronation Gospels&amp;nbsp;may have been produced in A
2 CONC achen.&lt;sup style="line-height: 1; font-size: 11.1999998092651px; unicode-bidi: -webkit-isolate;"&gt;[29]&lt;/sup&gt;&amp;nbsp;In addition, quantities of the other texts in the court library were also produced locally. During the reign of&amp;nbs
2 CONC p;Louis the Pious&amp;nbsp;(814-840), substantial quantities of ancient texts were produced at Aachen, including legal manuscripts such as the (leges scriptorium group),&amp;nbsp;patristic&amp;nbsp;texts including the five manuscripts of the&amp;nb
2 CONC sp;Bamberg Pliny Group.&lt;sup style="line-height: 1; font-size: 11.1999998092651px; unicode-bidi: -webkit-isolate;"&gt;[29]&lt;/sup&gt;&amp;nbsp;Finally, under&amp;nbsp;Lothair I&amp;nbsp;(840-855), texts of outstanding quality were still being pr
