2 CONC : inherit;"&gt;Aachen became attractive as a spa by the middle of the 17th century, not so much because of the effects of the hot springs on the health of its visitors but because Aachen was then &amp;ndash; and remained well into the 19th centur
2 CONC y &amp;ndash; a place of high-level prostitution in Europe. Traces of this hidden agenda of the city's history is found in the 18th-century guidebooks to Aachen as well as to the other spas; the main indication for visiting patients, ironically, wa
2 CONC s&amp;nbsp;syphilis; only by the end of the 19th century had rheumatism become the most important object of cures at Aachen and Burtscheid. Aachen was chosen as the site of several important congresses and peace treaties: the&amp;nbsp;first congres
2 CONC s of Aachen&amp;nbsp;(often referred to as the&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;Congress of Aix-la-Chapelle&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;in English) on May 2, 1668,&lt;sup style="line-height: 1; font-size: 11.1999998092651px; unicode-bidi: -webkit-isolate;"&gt;[32]&lt;/s
2 CONC up&gt;&amp;nbsp;leading to the&amp;nbsp;First Treaty of Aachen&amp;nbsp;in the same year which ended the&amp;nbsp;War of Devolution.&lt;sup style="line-height: 1; font-size: 11.1999998092651px; unicode-bidi: -webkit-isolate;"&gt;[33]&lt;/sup&gt;&am
