2 CONC er between Germany, Belgium and the Netherlands&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin: 0.5em 0px; line-height: inherit;"&gt;Aachen lies on the&amp;nbsp;tripoint&amp;nbsp;of Germany, the Nether
2 CONC lands, and Belgium in the middle of theMeuse&amp;ndash;Rhine Euroregion, which contains an open valley basin and includes tributaries of the&amp;nbsp;Wurm&amp;nbsp;and the&amp;nbsp;Rur&amp;nbsp;rivers. The city is located in the basin of the&amp;nb
2 CONC sp;Meuse, directly on the northern edge of the&amp;nbsp;Eifel&amp;nbsp;region of the&amp;nbsp;Rhenish Massif, about 30 kilometres (19 miles) north of the&amp;nbsp;High Fens.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin: 0.5em 0px; line-height: inherit
2 CONC ;"&gt;The highest point of Aachen measures 410&amp;nbsp;m&amp;nbsp;Normalnull&amp;nbsp;(NN) and lies in the far southeast of the city. The lowest point is 125&amp;nbsp;m NN and is located in the north, on the border with the Netherlands. The lengt
2 CONC h of the city border is 87.7&amp;nbsp;km (54.5&amp;nbsp;mi), 23.8&amp;nbsp;km (14.8&amp;nbsp;mi) of which border Belgium and 21.8&amp;nbsp;km (13.5&amp;nbsp;mi) border the Netherlands. From north to south, the city is 21.6&amp;nbsp;km (13.4&amp;nbs
2 CONC p;mi) at its widest, and from east to west, it is 17.2&amp;nbsp;km (10.7&amp;nbsp;mi).&lt;sup style="line-height: 1; font-size: 11.1999998092651px; white-space: nowrap;"&gt;[&lt;em&gt;&lt;span title="This claim needs references to reliable sources
