2 CONC pan class="mw-editsection-bracket" style="margin-left: 0px; color: #555555; margin-right: 0px;"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin: 0.5em 0px; line-height: inherit;"&gt;As the westernmost city in Germany&lt;sup style="li
2 CONC ne-height: 1; font-size: 11.1999998092651px; unicode-bidi: -webkit-isolate;"&gt;[3]&lt;/sup&gt;&amp;nbsp;(and close to the Low Countries), Aachen and the surrounding area belongs to a&amp;nbsp;temperate climate zone, with humid weather, mild winter
2 CONC s, and warm summers. Because of its location north of the&amp;nbsp;Eifel&amp;nbsp;and the&amp;nbsp;High Fens&amp;nbsp;and its subsequent prevailing westerly weather patterns, rainfall in Aachen (on average 805&amp;nbsp;mm/year) is comparatively hig
2 CONC her than, for example,&amp;nbsp;Bonn&amp;nbsp;(with 669&amp;nbsp;mm/year). Another factor in the local weather forces of Aachen is the occurrence of&amp;nbsp;Foehn winds&amp;nbsp;on the southerly air currents, which results from the city's geograph
2 CONC ic location on the northern edge of the Eifel.&lt;sup style="line-height: 1; font-size: 11.1999998092651px; unicode-bidi: -webkit-isolate;"&gt;[47]&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin: 0.5em 0px; line-height: inherit;"&gt;Becaus
2 CONC e the city is surrounded by hills, it suffers from&amp;nbsp;inversion-related&amp;nbsp;smog. Some areas of the city have become&amp;nbsp;Urban heat islands&amp;nbsp;as a result of poor heat exchange, both because of the area's natural geography, a
2 CONC s well as from human activity. The city's numerous cold air corridors, which are slated to remain as free as possible from new construction, therefore plays an important role in the urban climate of Aachen.&lt;sup style="line-height: 1; font-size
2 CONC : 11.1999998092651px; unicode-bidi: -webkit-isolate;"&gt;[48]&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin: 0.5em 0px; line-height: inherit;"&gt;The January average is 3.0&amp;nbsp;&amp;deg;C (37&amp;nbsp;&amp;deg;F), while the July averag
2 CONC e is 18.5&amp;nbsp;&amp;deg;C (65&amp;nbsp;&amp;deg;F). Precipitation is almost evenly spread throughout the year.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line /><line>&lt;tbody&gt;</line><line>&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th style="border: 1px solid #aaaaaa; padding: 0.2em 0.4em; back
