1 _OID 82afdaf7-49ae-446d-9065-4fc83e9602c6
1 DATE 1605-1710
1 PLAC Port Royal (Acadia), Nova Scotia, Canada
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: trebuchet ms,geneva; font-size: medium;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Port Royal (Acadia)&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: trebuchet ms,geneva; font-size: medium;"&gt;(pr
2 CONC esent-day Annapolis Royal, Nova Scotia) was founded in 1632, almost twenty years after Habitation at Port Royal was destroyed. The Habitation at Port Royal was established by France in 1605 and was that nation's first successful settlement in Nort
2 CONC h America.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: trebuchet ms,geneva; font-size: medium;"&gt;Port Royal served as the capital of Acadia until its destruction by British military forces in 1613. France relocated th
2 CONC e settlement and capital 8&amp;nbsp;km (5.0&amp;nbsp;mi) upstream and to the south bank of the Annapolis River. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: trebuchet ms,geneva; font-size: medium;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: trebuchet ms,geneva
2 CONC ; font-size: medium;"&gt;The relocated settlement kept the same name "Port Royal" and served as the capital of Acadia for the majority of the 17th century until the British conquest of the colony in 1710, at which time the (relocated) settlement wa
2 CONC s renamed to Annapolis Royal.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: trebuchet ms,geneva; font-size: medium;"&gt;Port Royal was the primary Acadian settlement until Acadians migrated out of the communi
2 CONC ty to Pisiguit, Cobequid, Grand-Pr&amp;eacute;, and Beaubassin (Isthmus of Chignecto) in the 1680s. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
