2 TITL William Eilola Obituary
1 _OID 8f7cf70f-346f-4cc0-b42a-5238ffc8e5f5
1 DATE 2010
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;Hancock: William T. Eilola, 83, of Hancock, passed away on Thursday evening, October 7, 2010 shortly after admission to Portage Health Care in Hancock.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; Bill was born on July 16, 1927 in Hanco
2 CONC ck to the late William A. and Ruth (Miller) Eilola. He graduated from Hancock High School in 1945. He then served in the United States Navy from 1945 to 1946 before graduating from the University of Michigan in 1950 with a Bachelors Degree in Busin
2 CONC ess Administration.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; On August 24, 1953 he was united in marriage to Jeanne O'Brien. They celebrated their 57th anniversary this year.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; Bill was employed at Thomas Ristell &amp;amp; Company in Houghton from 195
2 CONC 0 to 1961. He was then employed at Michigan Tech University from 1961 until retirement in 1988 where he served as Budget Officer and Assistant Treasurer.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; Bill was preceded in death by his parents; his step-father, Ernest Neva; h
2 CONC is sister, Mary Kitchen; and son-in-law, David Niemeyer.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; He is survived by his wife, Jeanne; 4 children: Sara Niemeyer of Rochester, NY, Susan Eilola of Grand Rapids, Bill (Colleen) Eilola of Sault Ste. Marie, and Paula (Bob) Nu
2 CONC tini of Hancock; grandchildren: Laura, Rachel, and Eric Niemeyer, Joshua, Matthew, and Timothy Eilola, and Bella Nutini; brothers by choice, Dr. Leo Lindquist of Greenville, NC: brothers-in-law: Jim O'Brien of Hancock and Marlin (Jane) Kitchen of M
2 CONC arquette; sisters-in-law: Helen (Norbert) Verville of Oskar and Patricia Seline of San Diego; cousin, Henry Fredd of Hancock; special friend and golfing pal, Bill Lucier of Hancock; and by nieces, nephews, and cousins.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; He wa
2 CONC s a member of the First United Methodist Church in Hancock. He served on the Hancock Public School Board for 20 years, and the Hancock Public Schools Foundation. He was a member of the U of M Alumni Association, the Presidents Society at MTU, the A
2 CONC lferd Erickson American Legion Post 186 of Hancock, and the Portage Lake Golf Course. He was also inducted to the H.C.H. Athletic Hall of Fame in 2010.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; A memorial service will be held at 11 A.M. on Tuesday, October 12, 2010 at t
2 CONC he First United Methodist Church with Rev. Amy Terhune to officiate. Interment will be in Hancock's Lakeside Cemetery, where the American Legion Post will hold military honors.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; Friends may call from 6 until 8 P.M. on Monday at t
2 CONC he O'Neill-Dennis Funeral Home in Hancock and for an hour before the services at the church on Tuesday.Online condolences may be made at www.oneilldennisfh.com. Memorials in lieu of flowers may be made to the Hancock Public Schools Foundation, 50
2 CONC 1 Campus Drive, Hancock, MI 49930 in the name of William Eilola.&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
