1 _OID d761bb53-17fd-4254-b39d-30a368af1e22
1 DATE 742-814 AD
1 PLAC Europe, Roman Empire
1 _DSCR Charlemagne (/ˈʃɑrlɨmeɪn/; 2 April 742/747/748[1] – 28 January 814), also known as Charles the Great (German: Karl der Große;[2] Latin: Carolus or Karolus Magnus) or Charles I, was the King of the Franks from 768, the King of Italy from 774, and fr
2 CONC om 800 the first emperor in western Europe since the collapse of the Western Roman Empire three centuries earlier. The expanded Frankish state he founded is called the Carolingian Empire.
