2 TITL Pierre Miville "Aka - LeSuisse - The Swiss"
1 _OID dc5ad8b8-0ec5-4e46-bb0b-12c996ae8800
1 DATE 1605 - October 14 1669
1 PLAC Notre Dame De Quebec Basilica-Cathedral 
1 _DSCR Burial:
2 CONT Notre Dame De Quebec Basilica-Cathedral 
2 CONT Quebec
2 CONT Capitale-Nationale Region
2 CONT Quebec, Canada 
2 CONT  
2 CONT Created by: AJ
2 CONT Record added: Jan 11, 2014 
2 CONT Find A Grave Memorial# 123169945 
2 CONT 
2 CONT Pierre Miville was known as Pierre Miville dit le Suisse, because he was from Switzerland. He moved to La Rochelle, France in 1646, and he leased land on the terraces, near the walls of Saint-Nicolas and the gate of la Verite from Pierre Maloisea
2 CONC u (a master blacksmith).
2 CONT 
2 CONT Pierre left France on 29 May 1649, with his wife and six children who were between 9 and 16 years old, sailing on the Grand Cardinal. They became well established in Quebec, but Pierre traveled back to France in Oct 1655 and returned to Quebec on 2
2 CONC 0 May 1656.
2 CONT 
2 CONT They settled in Lauzon, on the banks of the St Lawrence River. They had been preceded to the coast of Lauzon only by Francois Bissot, Guillaume Couture, and the Jesuits. It was a dangerous area for settlers, because of problems with the Iroquois an
2 CONC d the Hurons.
2 CONT 
2 CONT Pierre became a ship builder and was known for the quality of his ships. He wore himself out wanting to produce the best ships in New France. He died in his house on the Lauzon Coast, but his funeral and burial took place the next day in Quebec i
2 CONC n the parish cemetery.
2 CONT 
1 _META <metadataxml><cemetery /><transcription /></metadataxml>
